.TH FETCH 1
.SH NAME
fetch, curl, wget \- get a URL over HTTP or HTTPS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fetch
.RB [ \-v ]
.RB [ \-k ]
.RB [ \-o
.IR file ]
.I url
.br
.B curl
.RB [ \-v ]
.RB [ \-k ]
.RB [ \-o
.IR file ]
.I url
.br
.B wget
.RB [ \-k ]
.RB [ \-O
.IR file ]
.I url
.br
.B fetch \-i
.br
.B fetch \-p
.I host
.RI [ count ]
.br
.B fetch \-r
.I host
.br
.B fetch \-l
.I port
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fetch
gets the body of an
.B http://
or
.B https://
URL and shows it on the screen, or writes it into a file. HTTPS speaks
TLS 1.3 or 1.2: the server's certificate chain is followed to one of the
trusted roots in
.IR /etc/ssl/roots ,
every signature checked, its dates checked against the clock chip's date
and its name against the certificate's names.
.PP
.B fetch
is one program with many names: the network's everyday commands
.RB ( ping ,
.BR host ,
.BR nslookup ,
.BR ifconfig ,
.BR netstat ,
.BR traceroute ,
.BR nc ,
.BR curl ,
.BR wget )
are symbolic links to
.IR /bin/fetch ,
and the name it was started by says which command it is.
.B curl
is the same as
.BR fetch .
.B wget
writes into a file named as the URL's last part, else
.IR index.html .
.PP
When the body goes into a file (or with
.BR \-v ),
the size, the time and the speed are printed at the end.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-v
Also print the HTTP status, the headers and the TLS cipher.
.TP
.B \-k
Do not check the server's certificate (tests only).
.TP
.BI \-o " file\fR, " \-O " file"
Write the body into
.I file
instead of the screen.
.TP
.B \-i
The older name of
.BR ifconfig (1).
.TP
.BI \-p " host " \fR[\fIcount\fR]
The older name of
.BR ping (1)
(3 pings by default).
.TP
.BI \-r " host"
The older name of
.BR host (1).
.TP
.BI \-l " port"
Answer one HTTP request on
.I port
with a short text, then end (a test; it waits at most a minute).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 on a network error or an HTTP status of 400 or more;
2 for a usage error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/ssl/roots
The trusted root certificates (Mozilla's list, in DER).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
fetch https://example.com/
wget https://example.com/notes.txt
curl \-v \-o page.html https://example.com/
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ping (1),
.BR host (1),
.BR ifconfig (1),
.BR netstat (1),
.BR traceroute (1),
.BR nc (1),
.BR netd (4)
.SH BUGS
Only GET; no resumption of TLS sessions.
